course: dictionary
lesson: 15596
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word tagger is one of them, so you need the words around it to know which meaning the writer means. «The tagger ran after her across the playground» tells you it is a game, because of ran after and playground.
explain: «The tagger sprayed his name in big letters on the bus shelter.» Here a tagger is a person who writes their nickname on walls or trains, and that is illegal. The clues are sprayed and bus shelter. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap it into the sentence to check.
explain: «The computer's tagger labelled every word as a noun, verb or adjective.» This tagger is a computer program. Computers cannot read like we do, so the program labels each word for them. The clues are computer and labelled words.
fact: Tagger is a noun, and it can mean a person, a computer program or a tool.
fact: A graffiti tagger sprays or writes their nickname or sign on walls, trains or buildings, often without permission. This is illegal vandalism.
fact: In the playground game of tag, the tagger is the player who chases and touches the others. In the UK this game is called tig, or it.
fact: A part-of-speech tagger is a computer program that labels each word in a sentence, for example as a noun, verb or adjective.
fact: A tagger can also be a person or a tool that attaches tags or labels, such as tags on clothes or on animals.
exercise: «The tagger ran after her across the playground.» What does tagger mean here? | A computer program that labels words | *The player who chases and touches the others | A person who sprays names on walls | A tool that sticks labels on clothes
exercise: «The tagger sprayed his name on the train, and the police came.» What does tagger mean? | The player who chases in a game | A computer that reads sentences | *Someone who sprays a nickname or sign on trains and walls | A worker who sews labels into jackets
exercise: «The computer's tagger labelled each word as a noun or a verb.» Which clue shows tagger means a computer program? | the word tagger | the word noun | *labelled each word | the word verb
test: «The farmer used a tagger to put a tag on each lamb's ear.» What is the tagger here? | A program that labels words | A person who sprays walls | A player in a game | *A tool that attaches tags
test: In the playground, Sam shouts, «You're the tagger, so chase us!» What does tagger mean? | A graffiti artist | A label on a shirt | A computer program | *The player who chases and touches the others
exam: Which sentence uses tagger to mean a person who sprays a sign on a wall without permission? | «The tagger chased the other children round the field» | «The tagger sprayed his sign on the wall at night» | *«The tagger was a graffiti artist who painted the wall at night with permission» | «The tagger tagged the lambs with bright yellow tags»
